rlin/images/import_17/201601/29193636237.jpg"/><edm:provider rdf:resource="http://data.europeana.eu/organization/1482250000004671142"></edm:provider><edm:rights rdf:resource="http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/"/><edm:intermediateProvider rdf:resource="http://data.europeana.eu/organization/1482250000004510547"></edm:intermediateProvider></ore:Aggregation><ore:Proxy rdf:about="http://data.europeana.eu/proxy/europeana/2064129/Museu_ProvidedCHO_museum_digital_9133__technical_number_"><dc:creator xml:lang="en">Northern German Wagon Building Association</dc:creator><dc:description xml:lang="en">Starting in 1903, the Prussian state railways procured 23 D-train cars for course-car services, which lead three classes: a four-part, 1st class compartment, three six-part, second class compartments and three eight-part, third class compartments. There was also a service compartment, as well as one abortion for women and men. In 1904, the Breslauer Actien-Gesellschaft für Die Die delivered the “Danzig 0674” car for 44.103 marks. In 1906 the manufacturer donated a model to the Berlin Museum of Transport and Construction.&lt;br/>
&lt;br/>
